\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Permutation feature importance for XGBoost baseline ensemble on 2024 holdout (281 games). Market delta and spread dominate (0.24 and 0.18 normalized importance), confirming market efficiency as the primary signal. Rolling EPA metrics and QB status contribute moderately, while weather and travel have minimal impact.}}{51}{figure.caption.320}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Canonical training window ablation study results (November 8, 2025). Four scenarios tested on 2025 hold-out set (148 games): (A) 2018--2024 strict (MAE: 48.1 yds), (B) 2018--2024 with H=4 exponential decay on 2015--2017 (MAE: 47.8 yds), (C) 2020--2024 current (MAE: 48.4 yds), (D) 2015--2024 dissertation baseline (MAE: 47.8 yds). Scenario B selected as canonical window based on statistical superiority over strict windows (p=0.003 vs A, p=0.007 vs C) and interpretable decay function. Error bars represent 95\% bootstrap confidence intervals. All production models retrained with this window for ensemble consistency.}}{59}{figure.caption.325}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces Feature importance comparison between XGBoost and BNN models across the top 15 features. Defensive situational features (dark blue) dominate XGBoost importance rankings, while BNN assigns more weight to vegas line bias and environmental factors. The divergence reflects differing model architectures: XGBoost captures non-linear interactions while BNN emphasizes uncertainty-informative features.}}{60}{figure.caption.378}%
