\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {O.1}{\ignorespaces BNN Investigation: Diminishing Returns Over Time. Progress score (0-10) measures cumulative advancement toward production-ready model. Multi-Output v1 (18 hours) achieved highest score (6/10) before data leakage discovery. Subsequent approaches showed negative marginal returns: each additional hour yielded less progress. By hour 76 (Conformal BNN), marginal progress approached zero, signaling optimal stopping point.}}{541}{figure.caption.3432}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {O.2}{\ignorespaces BNN Investigation Research Journey: Four-Act Narrative Structure. The investigation progressed from initial optimism (Multi-Output v1 strong training metrics) through repeated setbacks (5 consecutive failures) to strategic realization (diminishing returns) and ultimate abandonment. This freed resources for XGBoost v4, which achieved breakthrough results in 57\% less time. The arc illustrates that research progress is non-monotonic: sometimes the path forward requires stepping back.}}{545}{figure.caption.3450}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {P.1}{\ignorespaces Geometric interpretation of orthogonalization. Correlated features $\mathbf {x}_{\text {player}}$ and $\mathbf {x}_{\text {opp}}$ (blue, red vectors, $\rho = 0.42$) create confounding. Gram-Schmidt process projects $\mathbf {x}_{\text {player}}$ onto orthogonal complement of $\mathbf {x}_{\text {opp}}$, yielding uncorrelated features $\mathbf {u}_{\text {opp}}$ and $\mathbf {u}_{\text {player}}$ (green, orange vectors, $\rho = 0$).}}{550}{figure.caption.3482}%
